tiochus VII holds Mesopotamia, Babylonia and Media.","cp":"parthian-empire","cpn":"Parthian Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seleucid_Empire","c":2},{"y":-129,"t":"loss","x":"129: Antiochus VII dies and the east is lost again.","cp":"parthian-empire","cpn":"Parthian Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seleucid_Empire","c":3},{"y":-129,"t":"contest_end","x":"129: the Seleucid-Parthian campaign ends at Ecbatana.","cp":"parthian-empire","cpn":"Parthian Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seleucid_Empire","c":3},{"y":-129,"t":"vassal_end","x":"129: Judea stops paying tribute.","cp":"judea","cpn":"Judea","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seleucid_Empire","c":1},{"y":-126,"t":"loss","x":"126: Judea takes Seleucid land.","cp":"judea","cpn":"Judea","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hasmonean_dynasty","c":1},{"y":-110,"t":"loss","x":"110: 487 cells of Syria and Upper Mesopotamia go to Cliopatria's Parthian shape.","cp":"parthian-empire","cpn":"Parthian Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seleucid_Empire","c":1},{"y":-91,"t":"loss","x":"91: Judea takes more Seleucid land.","cp":"judea","cpn":"Judea","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hasmonean_dynasty","c":1},{"y":-83,"t":"loss","x":"83: Tigranes of Armenia takes Syria.","cp":"kingdom-of-armenia","cpn":"Kingdom of Armenia","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tigranes_the_Great","c":3},{"y":-69,"t":"gain","x":"69: a rump Seleucid kingdom is restored.","cp":"kingdom-of-armenia","cpn":"Kingdom of Armenia","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seleucid_Empire","c":2},{"y":-66,"t":"loss","x":"66: 31 cells of the southern marches go to the Nabataeans.","cp":"nabataeans","cpn":"Nabataean Kingdom","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seleucid_Empire","c":1},{"y":-64,"t":"loss","x":"64: Pompey annexes Syria.","cp":"roman-republic","cpn":"Roman Republic","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syria_(Roman_province)","c":3},{"y":-64,"t":"dissolve","x":"64: the Seleucid Empire ends.","cp":"roman-republic","cpn":"Roman Republic","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syria_(Roman_province)","c":3}],"wars":[{"name":"Babylonian War","from":-311,"to":-309,"outcome":"Seleucus keeps Babylon and wins the upper satrapies; 'All Antigonid forces were removed from Babylon by 308 BC.'","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wars_of_the_Diadochi"},{"name":"Seleucid-Mauryan war","from":-305,"to":-303,"outcome":"Mauryan victory: Seleucus cedes Arachosia, Gedrosia, Paropamisadae and perhaps Aria for 500 elephants and a marriage alliance.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seleucid%E2%80%93Mauryan_war"},{"name":"Battle of Ipsus","from":-302,"to":-301,"outcome":"Antigonus is defeated and killed; Lysimachus and Seleucus divide his Asian lands, Seleucus taking eastern Anatolia and northern Syria.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wars_of_the_Diadochi"},{"name":"Battle of Corupedium","from":-282,"to":-281,"outcome":"Lysimachus is killed; the Seleucids gain Anatolia; Seleucus is assassinated by Ptolemy Keraunos after crossing the Hellespont.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Corupedium"},{"name":"First Syrian War","from":-274,"to":-271,"outcome":"Ptolemaic victory: Ptolemy II holds Caria and most of Cilicia by 271.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syrian_Wars"},{"name":"Second Syrian War","from":-260,"to":-253,"outcome":"Concluded around 253 with Antiochus II's marriage to Ptolemy's daughter; Antiochus regained Miletus and Ephesus.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syrian_Wars"},{"name":"Third Syrian War","from":-246,"to":-241,"outcome":"Ptolemy III briefly occupies Antioch and wins Seleucia Pieria and the northern Syrian coast in the peace of 241.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Third_Syrian_War"},{"name":"Revolt of Molon","from":-222,"to":-221,"outcome":"Media and Persis revolt under Molon and Alexander in 222; the rebellion collapses in 221.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antiochus_III_the_Great"},{"name":"Revolt of Achaeus","from":-220,"to":-213,"outcome":"Achaeus takes the royal title in Asia Minor; Antiochus marches in 216, drives him into Sardis by 214; the citadel holds out until 213.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antiochus_III_the_Great"},{"name":"Fourth Syrian War","from":-219,"to":-217,"outcome":"Raphia (summer 217): Ptolemy IV wins and preserves his control of Coele-Syria; Seleucia Pieria stays Seleucid.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syrian_Wars"},{"name":"Fifth Syrian War","from":-202,"to":-195,"outcome":"Antiochus III completes the subjugation of Coele-Syria in 198; the treaty of 195 leaves it to him.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syrian_Wars"},{"name":"Eastern campaign of Antiochus III","from":-209,"to":-205,"outcome":"Arsaces II and Euthydemus make peace; the eastern kingdoms return to nominal obedience; Antiochus returns west by Seistan and Kerman in 206/5.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antiochus_III_the_Great"},{"name":"Roman-Seleucid war","from":-192,"to":-188,"outcome":"Roman victory at Magnesia (December 190); the Treaty of Apamea (188) takes the land north and west of the Taurus, 15,000 talents and the fleet.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman%E2%80%93Seleucid_war"},{"name":"Sixth Syrian War","from":-170,"to":-168,"outcome":"Antiochus IV occupies Egypt (Pelusium November 170; Thebes October 169), withdraws late 169, returns in 168 and leaves Egypt and Cyprus on Popillius's ultimatum at Eleusis.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syrian_Wars"},{"name":"Maccabean Revolt","from":-167,"to":-143,"outcome":"The Maccabees take Jerusalem at the end of 164; Judas is killed at Elasa in 160; 'By 143 BC' Judea is independent and the Acra falls in 141.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hasmonean_dynasty"},{"name":"Revolt of Timarchus","from":-161,"to":-160,"outcome":"'Demetrius defeated and killed Timarchus in 160 BC'.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demetrius_I_Soter"},{"name":"Parthian conquest of Media and Babylonia","from":-148,"to":-141,"outcome":"Mithridates I takes Media and Atropatene in 148/7 and Babylonia in 141; Elymais and Characene become Parthian vassals soon after.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mithridates_I_of_Parthia"},{"name":"Demetrius II's campaign against Parthia","from":-140,"to":-138,"outcome":"Demetrius II is captured in 138 (139 on the Seleucid Empire page) and held in Hyrcania.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mithridates_I_of_Parthia"},{"name":"Eastern campaign of Antiochus VII","from":-133,"to":-129,"outcome":"Antiochus VII recaptures Mesopotamia, Babylonia and Media, is killed at Ecbatana in 129 and the Parthians retake it all.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seleucid_Empire"},{"name":"Armenian conquest of Syria","from":-83,"to":-69,"outcome":"Tigranes invades Syria in 83 and ends the last Seleucid remnants; after Lucullus beats him at Tigranocerta in 69 a rump kingdom is restored.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tigranes_the_Great"},{"name":"Pompey's annexation of Syria","from":-66,"to":-64,"outcome":"Pompey annexes Syria in 64; Antiochus XIII is executed and Philip II deposed.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syria_(Roman_province)"}],"certainty":[{"from":-312,"to":-189,"level":"soft","note":"Ancient frontiers are approximate."},{"from":-188,"to":-129,"level":"soft","note":"The Anatolian frontier along the Taurus from Cape Sarpedon is fixed by the Treaty of Apamea and is the one sharp line; the Parthian frontier in Media and Babylonia moves with every campaign."},{"from":-128,"to":-64,"level":"soft","note":"A rump around Antioch with fluid frontiers against the Hasmoneans, the Nabataeans, the Parthians and Tigranes."}],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seleucid_Empire","title":"Seleucid Empire"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wars_of_the_Diadochi","title":"Wars of the Diadochi"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seleucid%E2%80%93Mauryan_war","title":"Seleucid-Mauryan war"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Corupedium","title":"Battle of Corupedium"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syrian_Wars","title":"Syrian Wars"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman%E2%80%93Seleucid_war","title":"Roman-Seleucid war"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mithridates_I_of_Parthia","title":"Mithridates I of Parthia"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Third_Syrian_War","title":"Third Syrian War"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antiochus_III_the_Great","title":"Antiochus III the Great"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tigranes_the_Great","title":"Tigranes the Great"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demetrius_I_Soter","title":"Demetrius I Soter"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hasmonean_dynasty","title":"Hasmonean dynasty"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syria_(Roman_province)","title":"Syria (Roman province)"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antiochus_IV_Epiphanes","title":"Antiochus IV Epiphanes"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atropatene","title":"Atropatene"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cilicia","title":"Cilicia"}]}